## AI-Powered Hyperlocal Services & Community Assistance Platform

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, AI engineer, product designer, database architect, security engineer and QA engineer.

Build a polished, functional, mobile-first web application named **ApnaLocal**, launching initially in **Jaunpur, Uttar Pradesh, India**.

Tagline: **“Har Zaroorat Ka Local Solution.”**

This is not a static landing page, UI mockup, or collection of disconnected demo screens. Build an integrated working MVP with functional customer, service-provider and admin workflows, persistent data, and meaningful AI-powered features.

If an existing ApnaLocal project is open, inspect and improve the existing project. Preserve useful existing work, reuse compatible components and avoid unnecessarily rewriting working code. If starting from scratch, establish a clean project architecture.

## 1. PRODUCT VISION

ApnaLocal solves everyday neighborhood problems by connecting residents with nearby, available, trustworthy service providers.

Examples:
- A leaking tap requires a plumber.
- A faulty switch requires an electrician.
- A broken chair needs a carpenter.
- A student needs a local tutor.
- Someone needs AC, RO, appliance, vehicle or mobile repair.
- A resident needs cleaning, pest control, beauty services or other household assistance.
- A user cannot find a provider and wants to publish a service request.
- A resident wants local recommendations or to post a lost-and-found notice.

Build a marketplace that supports small jobs, consultations, appointments, service requests and community assistance.

Primary language: English, with Hindi language support and an architecture that can support additional Indian languages later.

Currency: INR (₹). Timezone: Asia/Kolkata. Initial location: Jaunpur, Uttar Pradesh.

Never fabricate real users, real verification, real reviews or real availability. Clearly label seed records as demo data until genuine users and providers join.

