## 8. BOOKING AND AVAILABILITY ENGINE

The booking flow must work end to end.

1. Customer selects a provider and service.
2. Customer enters problem details and address.
3. Customer chooses an available date and slot.
4. Server validates provider status and service-area compatibility.
5. Server checks availability and existing bookings.
6. Customer confirms the request.
7. Booking is persisted.
8. Provider receives an in-app notification.
9. Provider accepts, rejects or proposes a new time.
10. Customer receives the updated status.
11. Accepted appointments are confirmed.
12. Provider can mark work in progress and completed.
13. Customer can review the completed service.

Clearly distinguish a booking request from a confirmed appointment.

Use server-authoritative timestamps. Apply appropriate cancellation rules and record status history.

If a payment gateway is not configured, do not collect real payment details. Display a clear "Pay directly to provider" or "Payment integration coming soon" label as appropriate.

